From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:57:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] nxpatch: rewrite compressed switch tables that dispatch
 through x18

Mush8 only handled br x18 at a hardcoded list of i32 jump tables (MK8DX).
Splatoon 3 11.3.0 has 110 such sites (main 102, sdk 8), all clang's
compressed form: adr x18, anchor; ldrb/ldrh wK, [xB, xI]; add x18, x18,
xK, lsl #2; br x18.

The new switch.rs detects that pattern and emits an O(1) dispatch through a
pad table (ldp s,t; b anchor+4e per entry). No flags or guest registers are
changed; out-of-range values trap with brk #0x18 instead of jumping wrong.
ldrb tables get all 256 pads; ldrh tables are decoded when adrp/add base and
cmp/b.hi bound are found, otherwise get the full 65536-entry range.
Known MK8 tables keep their original path. verify now reads jump targets
from Output::jump_targets for both kinds.

